\begin{itemize}
\item Hardy, Littlewood, and Pólya (1934): foundational convex analysis
\item Rockafellar (1970): formal convex function theory
\item Durrett (2019), Shreve (2004): applications in probability and finance
\item Extensions in martingale theory and stochastic processes
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Convexity means function lies below any supporting hyperplane
\item Expectation is a weighted average of random variable values
\item Inequality shows function of average \( \leq \) average of function values
\item Visualized as chord lying above curve for convex functions
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Bounding expectations in statistics
\item Risk assessment in economics and finance
\item Convex optimization problem analysis
\item Martingale theory: convex functions of martingales form submartingales
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Martingales model "fair game" sequences
\item Jensen's Inequality applied to conditional expectations
\item Convex functions of martingales are submartingales
\item Fundamental in financial mathematics and stochastic analysis
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Jensen's Inequality links convexity and expectation
\item Provides fundamental bounds in multiple fields
\item Plays a key role in martingale and stochastic process theory
\item Future work: infinite-dimensional extensions, machine learning applications
\end{itemize}
